WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.760
We ask a lot of questions
about our diet.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.080
What’s the right way to
treat a chronic illness?

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.720
Fight off a virus,
lose weight?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.640
The problem is, we get
a lot of different answers.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.880
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.760
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:26.120
People spend lots of time and effort
trying to keep their ears free of ear wax.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:31.400
It may not surprise you to know that
some methods work better than others.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.880
Ear candles
(also known as ear cones)

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.680
are promoted as a low cost,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.320
effective treatment for earwax.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.200
They're hollow tubes of fabric

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.000
impregnated with paraffin
or beeswax.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.840
One end is placed
in the entrance

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.320
to the ear canal
and the other end is lit.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.880
After 15 minutes or so,
the flame is extinguished,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.680
and a brownish waxy substance
can be seen

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.000
within the remaining stub.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.520
This is claimed to be earwax

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.240
drawn out by some sort of
vacuum "chimney effect."

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.720
But the same residue

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.840
(presumably
from the burning wax smoke)

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.480
appears if you burn it alone
outside the ear.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.480
Researchers actually took
the additional step

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.480
of running
used ear candle stubs

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.240
through a mass spectrometer,
and indeed,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.960
no evidence of earwax
was found.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.640
Not surprisingly, perhaps,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.200
since tympanometric
measurements showed

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.160
no signs of negative
"chimney effect" pressure

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.800
at any point.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.200
Not to be dissuaded,
proponents suggest

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.680
that while no earwax
may be drawn out that day,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.080
the candling process
at least heats up

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.120
and melts the earwax,
which then comes out naturally

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.920
over the next few days.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.520
But Health Canada measured
the air temperature

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.200
at the ear end
of the burning candle,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.560
and the highest temperature
reached

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.080
was only 72 degrees Fahrenheit,

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.240
well below body temperature.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.280
Though the purported theories
were found to be

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.600
"implausible
and demonstrably wrong,"

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.640
the only way to really tell
if it works

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.760
is to examine the wax buildup
in people

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.520
before and after ear candling.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.440
Photographs
inside the ear canal

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.680
were taken before and after
ear candling.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:12.040
Not only was no wax removed,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.880
but in some of the ear canals
candle wax was deposited.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.800
So they ended up worse
than they were before,

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.960
not to mention
the recorded complications,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.520
including ear burns,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.200
complete candle wax blockage
of ear canals,

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.760
eardrum perforation,
infection,

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.120
and setting people's hair
on fire.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.800
Researchers concluded,
"Ear candles have no benefit

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.480
in the management of earwax

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.720
and may result
in serious injury."

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.080
Ear candles appear
to be a triumph

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.120
of ignorance over science.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.480
So, what is effective
for getting rid of earwax?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.440
I'll cover that, next...

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.880
One of the most common
reversible causes

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.840
of hearing loss
is earwax buildup.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.160
Earwax is normal,
and if it isn't causing symptoms

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.760
should be left alone.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.720
It doesn't start interfering
with hearing acuity

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.560
until it clogs off

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.600
at least 80 percent
of the ear canal.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.000
Ironically, hearing aids
are a risk factor

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.720
for excessive earwax,

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.920
as are anything else you put
in your ear, like ear plugs,

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:21.000
since that stimulates
the earwax glands.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.960
For further irony,
so may cotton-tipped swabs

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.800
that as many as two-thirds
of people use

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.440
to clean their ears.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.800
You may think
you're making things better

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.160
by swabbing out your ears,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.040
but you may actually be
making them worse.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:39.720
Simply removing protective wax
can leave your ear canals dry,

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.440
itchy, and achy

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.440
or even lead to "Q-tip otalgia,"

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.160
a term coined
to refer to an ear pain syndrome

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.600
caused by cotton-tipped swabs.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.920
You shouldn't need to clean
your ear canals at all

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.840
because the wax should make
its way out on its own.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.480
That's right.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.120
Ears are self-cleaning.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.960
The lining of your ear canal
grows outward

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.960
from your eardrum,
so secreted earwax

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.000
and any dirt that's trapped

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.680
is eventually conveyor belted
out of the ear.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.840
However, this self-cleaning
mechanism can fail

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.840
in 1 in 20 younger adults

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.200
and in as many
as 1 in 3 older adults

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.680
and lead to excessive or
impacted earwax accumulation,

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.560
though they may not
even know it.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.040
Seventy percent
of those surveyed

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.400
who had both ears
completely blocked with wax

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.600
thought their hearing was good.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.160
But when their ears
were cleared,

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.680
they were suddenly able
to hear better.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.440
Clearing out impacted wax
can also improve symptoms

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.160
of ear irritation, pressure,
and fullness.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.760
So, what's the best way
to do it?

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.320
Q-tips are a no-no.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.120
Pushing anything
into the ear canal

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.840
can end up making things worse

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.760
by impacting wax
even deeper into the ear

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.800
or traumatizing the canal,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.720
resulting in abrasions,
infections,

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:03.320
or even, rarely,
eardrum perforation.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.200
There's even a case report
of a cotton swab causing

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:10.960
a brain abscess
and fatal meningitis,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.280
though the presence
of wood splinters

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.840
suggests the tip had broken off
inside the ear.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:20.080
Cotton swab packaging
already cautions users

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.040
against ear canal insertion,

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:25.520
but perhaps warning labels
should be made even clearer,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.640
wrote one clinical
medical officer:

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.640
"do not go near the ear hole

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.840
or avoid the ear altogether."

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.280
What about those ear drops
sold for wax removal?

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.120
There are about a dozen

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.080
different marketed formulations
on the market,

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.120
none of which appears to work
any better than any other,

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.840
or even compared to saline
(which is just salt water)

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:48.840
or plain tap water.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.480
But five days of treatment
does clear earwax

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.800
in about 1 in 5 cases
compared to only 1 in 20

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.760
that clear up on their own
within that time.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.760
At the very least,
those ear drops

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.600
may be able to soften wax

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:05.360
before bulb syringe irrigation.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.880
Irrigation
(also called ear syringing)

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.440
involves flushing out the wax

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.000
with a low-pressure jet of warm
(body temperature) water.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.320
It works up to 70 to 90 percent
of the time,

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.200
and if it doesn't,
clinicians have fancy devices

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:23.120
to manually remove the wax
under direct observation.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.440
The irrigation can be tried
at home, though.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.960
Researchers randomized
to use a bulb at home

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.760
had about a 50 percent
success rate

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.760
in clearing their obstruction,
and armed with this knowledge

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.680
were significantly less likely
to subsequently require

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.560
in-office irrigation.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.360
Significant complications
only happen

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:43.960
in approximately
1 in 1000 irrigations.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:48.440
You should not use
an oral water jet.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:49.840
There are papers with names like

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:55.560
"Catastrophic Otologic Injury From Oral Jet
Irrigation of the External Auditory Canal."

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.920
Even at one-third power,
Waterpiks were shown to be able

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:03.480
to perforate the eardrums
of fresh cadavers.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.040
Those who insist
on violating this advice

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.800
should at the very least
use the lowest setting,

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.680
use a tip
with multiple orifices,

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.800
and make sure the water stream
is directed

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.680
only against the walls
of the ear canal,

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.840
never straight back
towards the eardrum.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:22.120
But really, just don't do it.

